<body>

  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <div class="meta">
    <strong>Effective Date:</strong>"2026-06-25"
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      LifeGraph (“we”, “our”, or “the app”) is a personal data application that helps users synchronize,
      analyze, and visualize their health and fitness data. This includes optional integration with
      Google Health APIs to import user-authorized health and fitness information.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring transparency about how your data is used.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

    <h3>Google Health / Fitness Data (if connected)</h3>
    <p>When you connect your Google account, we may access:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Physical activity data (e.g., steps, workouts)</li>
      <li>Heart rate data (if available and authorized)</li>
      <li>Sleep data (if authorized)</li>
      <li>Other health-related metrics you explicitly grant access</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>App-Provided Data</h3>
    <p>We may also store:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>User-created fitness logs (e.g., workouts, body metrics)</li>
      <li>Preferences and configuration settings</li>
    </ul>

    <p>We do not collect data without your explicit consent or action.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How We Use Your Data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Synchronize health and fitness data</li>
      <li>Display trends and visualizations</li>
      <li>Generate personal insights</li>
      <li>Improve user experience within the app</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not use your data for advertising or marketing.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Data Storage</h2>
    <p>
      Your data is stored securely in your application’s backend or database.
      We take reasonable measures to protect it from unauthorized access.
      Data remains tied to your user account.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>We do not sell, rent, or share your personal health data with third parties.</p>
    <p>We only share data when necessary:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>With Google APIs to retrieve authorized data</li>
      <li>If required by law or legal process</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      LifeGraph uses Google Health / Fitness APIs for data synchronization.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google Privacy Policy:
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank">
        https://policies.google.com/privacy
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      We retain your data only as long as your account is active or needed to provide the service.
      You may request deletion of your data at any time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your Rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Access your data</li>
      <li>Request correction or deletion</li>
      <li>Revoke Google access via your Google Account settings</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      We implement reasonable security measures to protect your data, including secure authentication
      and restricted access controls. However, no system is 100% secure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy occasionally. Updates will be posted on this page with a new effective date.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, contact:
    </p>
